      {
        "id": 124578,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-12-30T22:07:07.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I play on advanced too, Unity does most of her damage on the front side, on the back she struggles, but really everyone struggles once they flip, and your heroes that need to build up should be ready to roll by then. &nbsp;A good start by Unity can have half of the Ennead dead by the time they flip.</p><p>A not so good start she can usually still do a good bit of damage before they flip.</p><p>Normally I get about 12 damage to all the ennead from Cryo-Bot before flip time, after that I tend to get less, but still add in a decent chunk of damage.</p><p>Scrap Metal is huge for unity, and not to be underrated is the sheer volume of equip cards she can throw out to protect other player's equipment.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 21,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:58:37.953Z",
