      {
        "id": 124580,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-01-06T20:02:44.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Well he not only destroys your equipment but hurts you for it. &nbsp;You keep your build more minimalist, holding onto search and recovery cards because you will need them and so on.</p><p>With Unity and the Ennead Flash Forge, Robot Reclamation and Scrap Metal become incredibly important cards. &nbsp;Volatile parts becomes a pretty good damage option while Raptor Bot becomes very situational and most of the time is not worth playing.</p><p>Changes like that are similar to changing how you would play AZ or Bunker vs. Omnitron, since you prioritize certain cards and abandon your \"get out all the cards\" strategy.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 23,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:58:38.080Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
